{
 "_note": "Course terrain for the app, written by tools/build-terrain.mjs from the game's own collision (Switch Sports Resort's since 2026-11-04, NSS's before: the field meshes with the six HoleCovers closing the cups; SR's water, H3's sea included, is in the field mesh, where NSS's H3 had the separate sea actor Object_BGOBJ_GolfCourse03Water, --nss-extras) by vertical ray casts through tools/nss-registration.json; read by src/terrain.js. hNN.bin: the ground height and surface class on a w x h grid over the 250x304 map frame (sample (i, j) = the map px square [2i, 2i+2) x [2j, 2j+2), its centre at ((i+0.5)/w, (j+0.5)/h)): the height the ray at the centre lands on, in ydPerUnit above the hole's datum (NSS y 0 = the WSR player start's height; datumY = it in WSR's KCL units, 0.1 m, datumYd in yd), nodata where no ground lies under it; the class the majority of 4x4 rays over the cell (classNames: the KCL vocabulary plus 17, sand OB; codeToClass maps the NSS surface codes). gNN.bin: heights over nss-truth.json's green box + margin at stepYd, in unitYd above z0Yd (the green's mean height above the datum), with a mask of the nodes whose ray lands on the green. Byte layouts in the tool's header; both files repeat their own sizes, datum, box and units in a header. classes: per-hole sample counts by class; noHeight: samples with no ground; collisionSha1: the dump files read; datumWsrMeshY: the WSR start's height in KCL units (tools/nss-pins.json), against datumY; missing (only on a build run with --allow-missing): the separate collision actors the hole was built without.",
 "source": "nss",
